 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed changes are pushed to browsers over sockets the service hosts itself, keeping delivery independent of a realtime vendor and giving subsecond updates; the team accepts connection-capacity and reconnect work in exchange. Five-second HTTPS polling and a hosted realtime service were the alternatives. Polling was the simplest stateless route but lagged by seconds and multiplied reads; the hosted service removed connection operations but added recurring fees and provider coupling. See `docs/decisions/change-delivery-transport.md`.
